; Real Metal dispatch against independent per-token lane dispatches.
; Q4_K/Q6_K/Q8_0 committed byte fixtures; F32 deterministic weights.
; Nine distinct inputs cross the eight-token tile; output pitch exceeds rows.
; Q4_K and Q6_K decode run the fused pair-of-rows kernels (qwen38-decode-quant.bml), across superblocks
; and an odd row count: row 0 sits within the door's named bound of the Form fp64 dot, every row answers
; row 0 byte for byte (identical rows, identical input), the serial reference sits within its own bound,
; and the output padding keeps its sentinel.
; F32 prefill floats must match byte-for-byte; Q8_0, Q4_K and Q6_K prefill run on the matrix unit
; (qmb-q80-mma / qmb-q4k-mma / qmb-q6k-mma: simdgroup_multiply_accumulate chooses its own association) and their
; floats must sit within the lane's named bound of the per-token lane's (each side within one bound of the exact
; sum, |w x| from the K-quant weights through q4m-flat-at / q6m-flat-at); padding must retain its sentinel.
; Bit 32: the lane's K-quant tile (pipelines 52/53, the weights decoded one sub-block a K step) answers the
; per-weight attestant tile (qmb-quant-mma, emitted here) byte for byte, padding included, every slot written,
; the attestant's first token not all zero; both dispatches come back and the four buffers free. Two fixtures:
;   the committed superblocks in rows of eight (superblock s of row r is the fixture's (r >> s) & 1, so rows
;   0..255 differ): Q4_K and Q6_K, 3 and 257 rows (one and nine row tiles), 9 and 33 tokens (one and two token tiles);
;   edge pools that meet every exponent a finite half holds, 0 (the subnormals) through 30 (the largest finite), in
;   both signs, 0x0001 0x03ff 0x0400 0x7bff and their negatives among them, each where its term stands alone. Q4_K
;   (165): d at each exponent in each sign with dmin a signed zero, dmin at each in each sign with d a signed zero, both
;   in one binade, and named edges (zeros of both signs, 0x7bff / 0xfbff over twelve 0xff scale bytes and nibbles 15, a
;   huge d over nibbles 0 so a subnormal dmin answers alone, scale bytes whose high bits alone carry sub-blocks 4..7),
;   sc and mn across 0..63 at sub-blocks 0..3 and at 4..7 (through their high bits). Q6_K (70): d at each exponent of
;   both signs, scale bytes across all 256 (-128 and 127 among them), quants across -32..31 and whole superblocks of -32
;   and of 31. Rows of ONE superblock (cols 256: no larger neighbour's rounding swallows a small one's error) at 9 and 33
;   tokens, and rows of two pool neighbours (cols 512) at 33. The pools' coverage is read back from their bytes (Q4_K
;   through the body's q4m-scale / q4m-min) and is part of the bit. A half's sign x exponent cell (62: + 0..30, then
;   - 0..30) counts where the half stands alone in a superblock whose row of one answers the attestant a word that is not
;   a zero: a fault in that cell's sign negates a live word. Every cell of Q4_K's d, of its dmin and of Q6_K's d.
; Bit 64: the f16 identity the tile's equality rests on, on the device without a model, in the lane's own unit:
;   float(as_type<half>(h)) and q4k_f16(h) / q6k_f16(h) (the attestant's pow2 loop) agree bit for bit on all 63488
;   finite patterns, +0 (0x0000 -> 0x00000000) and -0 (0x8000 -> 0x80000000) among them; on the 2048 non-finite
;   patterns the pair parts, and the bit claims what each answers: as_type<half> +-inf at mantissa 0 and NaN at the
;   other 2046, the pow2 loop the finite +-2^16 (1 + m/1024), bits sign | 0x47800000 | m << 13. How the NaNs read
;   (payload kept, quieted, or the canonical 0x7fc00000) is printed, not claimed. The probe's three buffers start as
;   0x5a5a5a5a, a finite word none of these checks accepts, so a pattern it leaves unwritten reads short.
; Bit 128: q38-mv-batch-y refuses a Q4_K or Q6_K view whose cols is not a multiple of 256 aloud (q38pq-whole-refusal)
;   before anything is enqueued: the attempt answers nothing, the dispatch count and the output's sentinel hold;
;   the lane's widths read whole and a Q8_0 view is not this refusal's.
; Bit 256: rows of the lane's real widths, 20, 24 and 68 superblocks (cols 5120, 6144 and 17408: the ffn_down rows hold
;   68), 33 rows and 33 tokens (two tiles of each), Q4_K and Q6_K. The edge pools laid end to end (superblock s of row r
;   is pool[(r * width + s) mod n], width the row's superblocks) answer the attestant byte for byte. An exact world (d
;   and dmin 0x3c00, Q6_K's scales in -29..29, activations +-1) answers the attestant AND the scalar reference (pipelines
;   1 / 3: one thread a row, the serial fold, a dispatch a token) byte for byte: the tile's shared frame, its indexing and
;   its accumulation, seen at full width against arithmetic it does not share. Its exactness is read back from its bytes
;   through the body's decode (q4m-flat-at / q6m-flat-at): every weight an integer, the largest magnitude present times
;   the widest row's cols below 2^24, every activation word +-1, so every partial sum of a row, in any association, is an
;   integer below 2^24 and exact in f32. Its operands are exact in a half, so their precision is bit 512's.
; Bit 512: a one-hot world, where the exact world is blind to the frame's operands: every superblock zero but one a row,
;   and in it one weight, at local index (37 r + 11) mod 256 of superblock (7 r + 3) mod the row's: Q4_K d 0x3c01 x sc 63 x
;   nib 15 = 945.9228515625 and Q6_K d 0x3c01 x sc 127 x q 31 = 3940.8447265625 (20 and 22 significant bits: a half reads
;   946 and 3940), over 257 activations of full significand, +-pi (1 + (97 i mod 1021) / 1021) 2^(4 (i mod 9) - 16), among
;   a half's subnormals at the bottom and past its largest finite at the top. Every output is the one product fl32(w x),
;   exact in any association, so the tile answers the attestant AND the scalar reference byte for byte and every bit of
;   both operands shows: a frame that stages x through a half, holds ws as half or clamps x to +-1 reads short here while
;   bits 1, 2, 32 and 256 read full. Rows of 1, 20, 24 and 68 superblocks (33 rows, 33 tokens) and a tall shape, 4097 rows
;   of 20 at 33 tokens, Q4_K and Q6_K: the tall shape carries the superblock index and the output slot past 2^16 (81940
;   superblocks, 135300 slots), so an index narrowed to 16 bits reads short; the lane's real counts (348160 superblocks,
;   512 x 17408 outputs) are L1's to witness. The world is read back through the body's decode: each of the 256
;   one-weight superblocks holds that weight alone, at its index and of its value, a zero superblock none, and every
;   activation carries more than a half's eleven significant bits.
; Verdict 1023. Runs small fixture buffers only; no model admission or living state.
; preludes: native/metal/qwen35-dense-token-handle.fk form-stdlib/f16-decode.fk form-stdlib/lora-adapter.bml
(do
 (defn qpqb-repeat (text n acc) (if (le n 0) acc (qpqb-repeat text (sub n 1) (str_concat acc text))))
 (defn qpqb-input (n i acc)
  (if (ge i n) acc
   (qpqb-input n (add i 1) (str_concat acc (md-le32 (md-f32-bits (div (mul 1.0 (sub (mod (mul i 17) 257) 128)) 128.0)))))))
 ; Q8_0 runs on the matrix unit, which chooses its own association, so its floats answer to the
 ; lane's named bound rather than to the byte: each output within 2 * qmb-bound-coeff(cols) * 2^-24 *
 ; sum|w x| of the per-token lane's (both sit within one bound of the exact sum). The others still
 ; answer byte for byte.
 (defn qpqb-x (i) (div (mul 1.0 (sub (mod (mul i 17) 257) 128)) 128.0))
 (defn qpqb-s8 (v) (if (ge v 128) (sub v 256) v))
 (defn qpqb-w8 (ws cols r j)
  (do (let idx (add (mul r cols) j)) (let b (mul 34 (div idx 32)))
      (mul (fd-f16 (add (str_byte_at ws b) (mul 256 (str_byte_at ws (add b 1)))))
           (add (qpqb-s8 (str_byte_at ws (add b (add 2 (mod idx 32))))) 0.0))))
 (defn qpqb-abs (v) (if (lt v 0.0) (sub 0.0 v) v))
 (defn qpqb-absum (ws cols r t j acc)
  (if (ge j cols) acc (qpqb-absum ws cols r t (add j 1) (add acc (qpqb-abs (mul (qpqb-w8 ws cols r j) (qpqb-x (add (mul t cols) j))))))))
 (defn qpqb-f (s i) (ln-f32-decode (ln-u32-le s (mul 4 i))))
 (defn qpqb-near (ws cols rows t e a r)
  (if (ge r rows) 1
   (if (le (qpqb-abs (sub (qpqb-f a r) (qpqb-f e r)))
           (mul (mul 2.0 (mul (qmb-bound-coeff cols) 0.000000059604644775390625)) (add (qpqb-absum ws cols r t 0 0.0) 0.000000000001)))
    (qpqb-near ws cols rows t e a (add r 1)) 0)))
 ; the K-quant weight at flat index r*cols + j of the fixture tensor (rows contiguous, base 0), the body's own
 ; transcriptions; and the same near-bound check over them
 (defn qpqb-wk (type ws cols r j) (if (eq type 12) (q4m-flat-at ws 0 (add (mul r cols) j)) (q6m-flat-at ws 0 (add (mul r cols) j))))
 (defn qpqb-absum-k (type ws cols r t j acc)
  (if (ge j cols) acc (qpqb-absum-k type ws cols r t (add j 1) (add acc (qpqb-abs (mul (qpqb-wk type ws cols r j) (qpqb-x (add (mul t cols) j))))))))
 (defn qpqb-near-k (type ws cols rows t e a r)
  (if (ge r rows) 1
   (if (le (qpqb-abs (sub (qpqb-f a r) (qpqb-f e r)))
           (mul (mul 2.0 (mul (qmb-bound-coeff cols) 0.000000059604644775390625)) (add (qpqb-absum-k type ws cols r t 0 0.0) 0.000000000001)))
    (qpqb-near-k type ws cols rows t e a (add r 1)) 0)))
 (defn qpqb-agree (type ws cols rows t e a) (if (eq type 8) (qpqb-near ws cols rows t e a 0) (if (or (eq type 12) (eq type 14)) (qpqb-near-k type ws cols rows t e a 0) (if (str_eq e a) 1 0))))
 (defn qpqb-token (ps batch ref wh input rows cols pitch tokens t sentinel type ws)
  (if (ge t tokens) 1
   (do
    (let x (metal_buf_alloc (mul cols 4)))
    (let y (metal_buf_alloc (mul rows 4)))
    (let wrote (metal_buf_write x 0 (substring input (mul t (mul cols 4)) (mul (add t 1) (mul cols 4)))))
    (let enqueued (metal_enqueue ref (md-bind16 (list wh x y) (list rows cols) 256 0 0 0) (mul rows 32)))
    (let expected (metal_buf_read y 0 (mul rows 4)))
    (let actual (substring batch (mul t (mul pitch 4)) (mul 4 (add (mul t pitch) rows))))
    (let padding (substring batch (mul 4 (add (mul t pitch) rows)) (mul 4 (mul (add t 1) pitch))))
    (let released (add (metal_buf_free x) (metal_buf_free y)))
    (if (and (gt enqueued 0) (and (eq (qpqb-agree type ws cols rows t expected actual) 1) (str_eq padding sentinel)))
     (qpqb-token ps batch ref wh input rows cols pitch tokens (add t 1) sentinel type ws) 0))))
 (defn qpqb-shape (ps msl type weights rows cols refname bit)
  (do
   (let tokens 9) (let pitch (add rows 3))
   (let wh (metal_buf_alloc (str_len weights)))
   (let x (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul tokens cols) 4)))
   (let y (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul tokens pitch) 4)))
   (let input (qpqb-input (mul tokens cols) 0 ""))
   (let sentinel (qpqb-repeat (md-le32 (md-f32-bits 42.25)) 3 ""))
   (let w0 (metal_buf_write wh 0 weights))
   (let w1 (metal_buf_write x 0 input))
   (let w2 (metal_buf_write y 0 (qpqb-repeat (md-le32 (md-f32-bits 42.25)) (mul tokens pitch) "")))
   (metal_batch_concurrent)
   (let dispatched (q38-mv-batch-y ps (list wh rows cols type) x y tokens pitch 1))
   (let batch (metal_buf_read y 0 (mul (mul tokens pitch) 4)))
   (let ref (metal_pipeline msl refname))
   (let same (qpqb-token ps batch ref wh input rows cols pitch tokens 0 sentinel type weights))
   (let freed (sum (list (metal_buf_free wh) (metal_buf_free x) (metal_buf_free y))))
   (print (list "type" type "tokens" tokens "rows" rows "cols" cols "pitch" pitch "same-and-padding" same))
    (if (and (gt dispatched 0) same) bit 0)))
 ; Q4_K decode: the fused kernel's row 0 against the Form fp64 dot (q4m-* of q4k-msl.fk over the fixture row,
 ; S the unfused magnitude, the door's coefficient), every row byte-equal to row 0, and the serial reference
 ; within its own bound (coefficient cols, its fold depth)
 (defn qpqb-q4-b (idx) (mul 144 (div idx 256)))
 (defn qpqb-q4-j (i) (add (mul 2 (div i 64)) (div (mod i 64) 32)))
 (defn qpqb-q4-nib (ws idx)
  (do (let i (mod idx 256)) (let c (div i 64)) (let within (mod i 64)) (let hf (div within 32)) (let l (mod within 32))
      (let qb (q4m-qsb ws (qpqb-q4-b idx) (add (mul c 32) l)))
      (if (eq hf 0) (q4k-mod qb 16) (div qb 16))))
 (defn qpqb-q4-sp (ws idx) (mul (mul (q4m-d ws (qpqb-q4-b idx)) (q4m-scale ws (qpqb-q4-b idx) (qpqb-q4-j (mod idx 256)))) (qpqb-q4-nib ws idx)))
 (defn qpqb-q4-mp (ws idx) (mul (q4m-dmin ws (qpqb-q4-b idx)) (q4m-min ws (qpqb-q4-b idx) (qpqb-q4-j (mod idx 256)))))
 ; the parts by type: Q6_K has no min term (q6m-flat-at, stride 210)
 (defn qpqb-qk-sp (type ws idx) (if (eq type 12) (qpqb-q4-sp ws idx) (q6m-flat-at ws 0 idx)))
 (defn qpqb-qk-mp (type ws idx) (if (eq type 12) (qpqb-q4-mp ws idx) 0.0))
 (defn qpqb-qk-dot (type ws cols j acc) (if (ge j cols) acc (qpqb-qk-dot type ws cols (add j 1) (add acc (mul (sub (qpqb-qk-sp type ws j) (qpqb-qk-mp type ws j)) (qpqb-x j))))))
 (defn qpqb-qk-mag (type ws cols j acc) (if (ge j cols) acc (qpqb-qk-mag type ws cols (add j 1) (add acc (add (qpqb-abs (mul (qpqb-qk-sp type ws j) (qpqb-x j))) (qpqb-abs (mul (qpqb-qk-mp type ws j) (qpqb-x j))))))))
 (defn qpqb-qk-near? (got exact S coeff) (le (qpqb-abs (sub got exact)) (add (mul (mul coeff 0.000000059604644775390625) S) 0.000000000001)))
 (defn qpqb-qk-agree (type ws cols rows expected actual)
  (do (let exact (qpqb-qk-dot type ws cols 0 0.0)) (let S (qpqb-qk-mag type ws cols 0 0.0))
      (let got (qpqb-f actual 0)) (let ref (qpqb-f expected 0))
      (print (list "k-quant decode type" type "row 0: exact" exact "fused" got "serial" ref "fused dev/bound" (div (qpqb-abs (sub got exact)) (add (mul (mul (q38dq-bound-coeff cols) 0.000000059604644775390625) S) 0.000000000001))))
      (and (qpqb-qk-near? got exact S (q38dq-bound-coeff cols))
           (and (qpqb-qk-near? ref exact S cols)
                (str_eq (substring actual 0 (mul 4 rows)) (qpqb-repeat (substring actual 0 4) rows ""))))))
 (defn qpqb-decode (ps type fixture stride rows cols refindex)
  (do
   (let row (qpqb-repeat (read_file_slice fixture 0 (mul stride 2)) (div cols 512) ""))
   (let weights (qpqb-repeat row rows ""))
   (let wh (metal_buf_alloc (str_len weights)))
   (let x (metal_buf_alloc (mul cols 4)))
   (let y (metal_buf_alloc (mul (add rows 1) 4)))
   (let z (metal_buf_alloc (mul (add rows 1) 4)))
   (let sentinel (md-le32 (md-f32-bits 42.25)))
   (let writes (list (metal_buf_write wh 0 weights) (metal_buf_write x 0 (qpqb-input cols 0 ""))
    (metal_buf_write y 0 (qpqb-repeat sentinel (add rows 1) ""))
    (metal_buf_write z 0 (qpqb-repeat sentinel (add rows 1) ""))))
   (metal_batch_concurrent)
   (let reference (metal_enqueue (nth ps refindex) (md-bind16 (list wh x y) (list rows cols) 256 0 0 1) rows))
   (let dispatched (q38-mv ps (list wh rows cols type) x z 1))
   (let expected (metal_buf_read y 0 (mul (add rows 1) 4)))
   (let actual (metal_buf_read z 0 (mul (add rows 1) 4)))
   (let same (and (if (or (eq type 12) (eq type 14)) (qpqb-qk-agree type weights cols rows expected actual) (str_eq expected actual)) (str_eq (substring actual (mul rows 4) (str_len actual)) sentinel)))
   (let freed (sum (list (metal_buf_free wh) (metal_buf_free x) (metal_buf_free y) (metal_buf_free z))))
   (print (list "decode-type" type "rows" rows "cols" cols "same-and-padding" same "freed" freed))
   (and (and (gt reference 0) (gt dispatched 0)) (and same (eq freed 4)))))
 ; bit 32: text n times by doubling (the inputs here run to 67584 floats); bit s of r
 (defn qpqb-rep2 (text n) (if (le n 0) "" (if (eq (mod n 2) 0) (qpqb-rep2 (str_concat text text) (div n 2)) (str_concat text (qpqb-rep2 (str_concat text text) (div n 2))))))
 (defn qpqb-bit (r s) (if (eq s 0) (mod r 2) (qpqb-bit (div r 2) (sub s 1))))
 ; row r: eight superblocks, the s-th the fixture's superblock (r >> s) & 1; written one row at a time
 (defn qpqb-tile-row (sb stride r s acc)
  (if (ge s 8) acc
   (qpqb-tile-row sb stride r (add s 1) (str_concat acc (substring sb (mul stride (qpqb-bit r s)) (mul stride (add (qpqb-bit r s) 1)))))))
 (defn qpqb-tile-put (wh sb stride rows r)
  (if (ge r rows) wh
   (do (let w (metal_buf_write wh (mul r (mul 8 stride)) (qpqb-tile-row sb stride r 0 "")))
       (qpqb-tile-put wh sb stride rows (add r 1)))))
 ; a pool's row r: its superblocks s are pool[(r * rstep + s * step) mod n] (rstep 1 and step 0 keep a row to one
 ; superblock; rstep the row's own superblocks and step 1 lay the pool end to end, row after row)
 (defn qpqb-pool-row (pool n nsb rstep step r s acc)
  (if (ge s nsb) acc (qpqb-pool-row pool n nsb rstep step r (add s 1) (str_concat acc (nth pool (mod (add (mul r rstep) (mul s step)) n))))))
 (defn qpqb-pool-put (wh pool n stride nsb rstep step rows r)
  (if (ge r rows) wh
   (do (let w (metal_buf_write wh (mul r (mul nsb stride)) (qpqb-pool-row pool n nsb rstep step r 0 "")))
       (qpqb-pool-put wh pool n stride nsb rstep step rows (add r 1)))))
 ; every (token, row) slot of the output was written: none still holds the sentinel
 (defn qpqb-written? (out pitch rows ntok t r sent)
  (if (ge t ntok) 1
   (if (ge r rows) (qpqb-written? out pitch rows ntok (add t 1) 0 sent)
    (if (str_eq (substring out (mul 4 (add (mul t pitch) r)) (mul 4 (add (add (mul t pitch) r) 1))) sent) 0
     (qpqb-written? out pitch rows ntok t (add r 1) sent)))))
 ; the first word where a and b differ (bisection over halves), -1 when they agree
 (defn qpqb-first-diff (a b lo hi)
  (if (str_eq (substring a (mul 4 lo) (mul 4 hi)) (substring b (mul 4 lo) (mul 4 hi))) -1
   (if (le (sub hi lo) 1) lo
    (do (let mid (div (add lo hi) 2)) (let left (qpqb-first-diff a b lo mid))
        (if (ge left 0) left (qpqb-first-diff a b mid hi))))))
 ; token t of the lane's batch b against the scalar reference sp (pipeline 1 / 3: one thread a row, its serial fold) over
 ; the same weights and token t's activations, word for word; the first token whose rows differ, -1 when none does
 (defn qpqb-scalar (sp wh xs b rows cols pitch ntok t)
  (if (ge t ntok) -1
   (do
    (let x (metal_buf_alloc (mul cols 4))) (let y (metal_buf_alloc (mul rows 4)))
    (let w (metal_buf_write x 0 (substring xs (mul t (mul cols 4)) (mul (add t 1) (mul cols 4)))))
    (let e (metal_enqueue sp (md-bind16 (list wh x y) (list rows cols) 256 0 0 0) rows))
    (let s (metal_sync))
    (let got (metal_buf_read y 0 (mul rows 4)))
    (let freed (add (metal_buf_free x) (metal_buf_free y)))
    (let row (substring b (mul 4 (mul t pitch)) (mul 4 (add (mul t pitch) rows))))
    (if (and (gt e 0) (str_eq got row))
     (qpqb-scalar sp wh xs b rows cols pitch ntok (add t 1))
     (do (let at (qpqb-first-diff got row 0 rows))
         (print (list "scalar reference differs: token" t "dispatched" e "row" at "scalar" (if (ge at 0) (ln-u32-le got (mul 4 at)) -1) "tile" (if (ge at 0) (ln-u32-le row (mul 4 at)) -1)))
         t)))))
 ; the attestant and the lane's dispatch over the weights in wh (rows x cols), the outputs word for word, the activations
 ; the period's 257 floats laid end to end; with a scalar pipeline sp (0: none) every token against it too. Answers (ok,
 ; the attestant's words).
 (defn qpqb-tile-run (ps old type wh rows cols ntok label period sp)
  (do
   (let pitch (add rows 3)) (let nout (mul ntok pitch))
   (let sent (md-le32 (md-f32-bits 42.25)))
   (let fill (qpqb-rep2 sent nout))
   (let xs (substring (qpqb-rep2 period (add (div (mul ntok cols) 257) 1)) 0 (mul 4 (mul ntok cols))))
   (let x (metal_buf_alloc (mul 4 (mul ntok cols))))
   (let yo (metal_buf_alloc (mul 4 nout)))
   (let yn (metal_buf_alloc (mul 4 nout)))
   (let writes (list (metal_buf_write x 0 xs) (metal_buf_write yo 0 fill) (metal_buf_write yn 0 fill)))
   (metal_batch_concurrent)
   (let eo (metal_enqueue old (md-bind16 (list wh x yo) (list rows cols ntok pitch) 256 0 1 0) (qmb-mma-groups rows ntok)))
   (let en (q38-mv-batch-y ps (list wh rows cols type) x yn ntok pitch 0))
   (let synced (metal_sync))
   (let a (metal_buf_read yo 0 (mul 4 nout)))
   (let b (metal_buf_read yn 0 (mul 4 nout)))
   (let st (if (gt sp 0) (qpqb-scalar sp wh xs b rows cols pitch ntok 0) -1))
   (let freed (sum (list (metal_buf_free wh) (metal_buf_free x) (metal_buf_free yo) (metal_buf_free yn))))
   (let at (qpqb-first-diff a b 0 nout))
   (let written (qpqb-written? b pitch rows ntok 0 0 sent))
   (let live (if (str_eq (substring a 0 (mul 4 rows)) (qpqb-rep2 (md-le32 0) rows)) 0 1))
   (print (list "k-quant tile" label "type" type "rows" rows "cols" cols "tokens" ntok "dispatched" eo en "first differing word" at
    "attestant" (if (ge at 0) (ln-u32-le a (mul 4 at)) -1) "tile" (if (ge at 0) (ln-u32-le b (mul 4 at)) -1) "written" written "live" live "freed" freed
    "scalar reference: first differing token" (if (gt sp 0) st "none run")))
   (list (and (and (gt eo 0) (gt en 0)) (and (lt at 0) (and (eq written 1) (and (eq live 1) (and (eq freed 4) (lt st 0)))))) a)))
 (defn qpqb-tile (ps old type sb stride rows ntok per)
  (qpqb-tile-run ps old type (qpqb-tile-put (metal_buf_alloc (mul rows (mul 8 stride))) sb stride rows 0) rows 2048 ntok "fixture" per 0))
 (defn qpqb-pool-tile (ps old type pool n stride rows cols ntok rstep step label per sp)
  (qpqb-tile-run ps old type (qpqb-pool-put (metal_buf_alloc (mul rows (mul (div cols 256) stride))) pool n stride (div cols 256) rstep step rows 0) rows cols ntok label per sp))
 ; ---- the edge pools ----
 (defn qpqb-u16 (v) (str_concat (byte_to_str (mod v 256)) (byte_to_str (div v 256))))
 (defn qpqb-u16at (s o) (add (str_byte_at s o) (mul 256 (str_byte_at s (add o 1)))))
 (defn qpqb-h (s e m) (add (mul s 32768) (add (mul e 1024) m)))
 (defn qpqb-fill (b n acc) (if (le n 0) acc (qpqb-fill b (sub n 1) (str_concat acc (byte_to_str b)))))
 ; the mantissa at exponent e: at 0 the smallest (a) or the largest (b) subnormal, at 1 the smallest normal, at 30
 ; the largest finite; elsewhere spread and nonzero, so a clamp at 2^15 or a flush below 2^-14 moves the weights
 (defn qpqb-ma (e) (if (eq e 0) 1 (if (eq e 1) 0 (if (eq e 30) 1023 (add (mod (mul e 397) 1023) 1)))))
 (defn qpqb-mb (e) (if (eq e 0) 1023 (if (eq e 1) 0 (if (eq e 30) 1023 (add (mod (add (mul e 211) 5) 1023) 1)))))
 ; bytes ((i * n + b) * k + c) mod 256 for b in 0..n-1: superblock i's own run of quant, high-bit or scale bytes
 (defn qpqb-run (i b n k c acc) (if (ge b n) acc (qpqb-run i (add b 1) n k c (str_concat acc (byte_to_str (mod (add (mul (add (mul i n) b) k) c) 256))))))
 ; Q4_K: sc_j = (27 i + 9 j + 5) mod 64 and mn_j = (45 i + 21 j + 17) mod 64 laid into get_scale_min_k4's twelve
 ; bytes: byte t (t < 4) is sc_t with sc_{t+4}'s high pair, byte t + 4 is mn_t with mn_{t+4}'s, byte t + 8 the two
 ; low nibbles of sc_{t+4} and mn_{t+4}
 (defn qpqb-sc (i j) (mod (add (mul i 27) (add (mul j 9) 5)) 64))
 (defn qpqb-mn (i j) (mod (add (mul i 45) (add (mul j 21) 17)) 64))
 (defn qpqb-scb (i t acc)
  (if (ge t 12) acc
   (qpqb-scb i (add t 1) (str_concat acc (byte_to_str
    (if (lt t 4) (add (qpqb-sc i t) (mul 64 (div (qpqb-sc i (add t 4)) 16)))
     (if (lt t 8) (add (qpqb-mn i (sub t 4)) (mul 64 (div (qpqb-mn i t) 16)))
      (add (mod (qpqb-sc i (sub t 4)) 16) (mul 16 (mod (qpqb-mn i (sub t 4)) 16))))))))))
 (defn qpqb-q4x (d dmin sc qs) (str_concat (qpqb-u16 d) (str_concat (qpqb-u16 dmin) (str_concat sc qs))))
 (defn qpqb-q4 (i d dmin) (qpqb-q4x d dmin (qpqb-scb i 0 "") (qpqb-run i 0 128 167 3 "")))
 ; family 0: d at exponent e, dmin a signed zero; 1: dmin at e, d a signed zero; 2: both at e; 3 and 4: families 0 and 1
 ; in the other sign (d's sign follows e in 0 and e + 1 in 3, dmin's e + 1 in 1 and e in 4), so each half stands alone at
 ; every sign x exponent cell
 (defn qpqb-q4fam (f e acc)
  (if (gt e 30) acc
   (qpqb-q4fam f (add e 1) (append acc (list
    (if (eq f 0) (qpqb-q4 e (qpqb-h (mod e 2) e (qpqb-ma e)) (mul (mod (div e 2) 2) 32768))
     (if (eq f 1) (qpqb-q4 (add 31 e) (mul (mod (add (div e 2) 1) 2) 32768) (qpqb-h (mod (add e 1) 2) e (qpqb-mb e)))
      (if (eq f 2) (qpqb-q4 (add 62 e) (qpqb-h (mod (div e 2) 2) e (mod (add (mul e 113) 7) 1024)) (qpqb-h (mod (div (add e 1) 2) 2) e (mod (add (mul e 331) 11) 1024)))
       (if (eq f 3) (qpqb-q4 (add 101 e) (qpqb-h (mod (add e 1) 2) e (qpqb-mb e)) (mul (mod (add (div e 2) 1) 2) 32768))
        (qpqb-q4 (add 132 e) (mul (mod (div e 2) 2) 32768) (qpqb-h (mod e 2) e (qpqb-ma e))))))))))))
 ; Q6_K: ql, qh and the sixteen signed scales from superblock i's own runs, d last
 (defn qpqb-q6x (ql qh sc d) (str_concat ql (str_concat qh (str_concat sc (qpqb-u16 d)))))
 (defn qpqb-q6 (i d) (qpqb-q6x (qpqb-run i 0 128 89 13 "") (qpqb-run i 0 64 53 29 "") (qpqb-run i 0 16 151 9 "") d))
 (defn qpqb-q6fam (f e acc)
  (if (gt e 30) acc
   (qpqb-q6fam f (add e 1) (append acc (list
    (if (eq f 0) (qpqb-q6 e (qpqb-h (mod e 2) e (qpqb-ma e))) (qpqb-q6 (add 31 e) (qpqb-h (mod (add e 1) 2) e (qpqb-mb e)))))))))
 ; coverage, read back from the pool's bytes: sets as strings of "0"/"1"
 (defn qpqb-mark (s v) (str_concat (substring s 0 v) (str_concat "1" (substring s (add v 1) (str_len s)))))
 (defn qpqb-ex (h) (mod (div h 1024) 32))
 (defn qpqb-zero? (h) (eq (mod h 32768) 0))
 ; a half's sign x exponent cell: + 0..30, then - 0..30
 (defn qpqb-sx (h) (add (mul (div h 32768) 31) (qpqb-ex h)))
 ; row k answers the attestant a word that is not a zero (+0 or -0) at some token t < ntok
 (defn qpqb-live? (a pitch k t ntok)
  (if (ge t ntok) 0
   (if (eq (mod (ln-u32-le a (mul 4 (add (mul t pitch) k))) 2147483648) 0) (qpqb-live? a pitch k (add t 1) ntok) 1)))
 ; Q4_K: (d's sign x exponent cells where dmin is a signed zero, dmin's where d is, both in live rows, sc at sub-blocks
 ; 0..3, sc at 4..7 (d nonzero), mn at 0..3, mn at 4..7 (dmin nonzero)), sc and mn through the body's q4m-scale / q4m-min;
 ; a holds the attestant's words over the pool in rows of one superblock (row k is superblock k), ntok tokens at the pitch
 (defn qpqb-q4cov-j (sb dz mz j cov)
  (if (ge j 8) cov
   (do (let sc (q4m-scale sb 0 j)) (let mn (q4m-min sb 0 j)) (let hi (ge j 4))
       (qpqb-q4cov-j sb dz mz (add j 1)
        (list (nth cov 0) (nth cov 1)
              (if (or dz hi) (nth cov 2) (qpqb-mark (nth cov 2) sc))
              (if (or dz (not hi)) (nth cov 3) (qpqb-mark (nth cov 3) sc))
              (if (or mz hi) (nth cov 4) (qpqb-mark (nth cov 4) mn))
              (if (or mz (not hi)) (nth cov 5) (qpqb-mark (nth cov 5) mn)))))))
 (defn qpqb-q4cov (pool k n cov a pitch ntok)
  (if (ge k n) cov
   (do (let sb (nth pool k)) (let d (qpqb-u16at sb 0)) (let m (qpqb-u16at sb 2))
       (let dz (qpqb-zero? d)) (let mz (qpqb-zero? m)) (let live (eq (qpqb-live? a pitch k 0 ntok) 1))
       (qpqb-q4cov pool (add k 1) n
        (qpqb-q4cov-j sb dz mz 0
         (list (if (and live (and mz (not dz))) (qpqb-mark (nth cov 0) (qpqb-sx d)) (nth cov 0))
               (if (and live (and dz (not mz))) (qpqb-mark (nth cov 1) (qpqb-sx m)) (nth cov 1))
               (nth cov 2) (nth cov 3) (nth cov 4) (nth cov 5)))
        a pitch ntok))))
 ; Q6_K: q at weight i of superblock sb, q6k_wi's nib + hi * 16 - 32
 (defn qpqb-p4 (g) (if (le g 0) 1 (mul 4 (qpqb-p4 (sub g 1)))))
 (defn qpqb-q6q (sb i)
  (do (let h (div i 128)) (let wi (mod i 128)) (let l (mod wi 32)) (let g (div wi 32))
      (let qlb (str_byte_at sb (add (mul h 64) (add l (mul (mod g 2) 32)))))
      (let nib (if (lt g 2) (mod qlb 16) (div qlb 16)))
      (let hi (mod (div (str_byte_at sb (add 128 (add (mul h 32) l))) (qpqb-p4 g)) 4))
      (sub (add nib (mul hi 16)) 32)))
 (defn qpqb-q6cov-q (sb i acc) (if (ge i 256) acc (qpqb-q6cov-q sb (add i 1) (qpqb-mark acc (add (qpqb-q6q sb i) 32)))))
 (defn qpqb-q6cov-s (sb s acc) (if (ge s 16) acc (qpqb-q6cov-s sb (add s 1) (qpqb-mark acc (str_byte_at sb (add 192 s))))))
 ; (d's sign x exponent cells in live rows, the scale bytes, the quants (q + 32), whole superblocks of -32 and of 31),
 ; d nonzero
 (defn qpqb-q6cov (pool k n cov a pitch ntok)
  (if (ge k n) cov
   (do (let sb (nth pool k)) (let d (qpqb-u16at sb 208))
       (qpqb-q6cov pool (add k 1) n
        (if (qpqb-zero? d) cov
         (list (if (eq (qpqb-live? a pitch k 0 ntok) 1) (qpqb-mark (nth cov 0) (qpqb-sx d)) (nth cov 0))
               (qpqb-q6cov-s sb 0 (nth cov 1)) (qpqb-q6cov-q sb 0 (nth cov 2))
               (if (str_eq (substring sb 0 192) (qpqb-fill 0 192 "")) 1 (nth cov 3))
               (if (str_eq (substring sb 0 192) (qpqb-fill 255 192 "")) 1 (nth cov 4))))
        a pitch ntok))))
 ; ---- bit 256: the real rows' widths ----
 ; bytes ((i * m + b) * k + c) mod md, plus off (mod 256), for b in 0..n-1: superblock i's own run, of period 256 in i
 ; when m * k is odd and md is 256
 (defn qpqb-runm (i m b n k c md off acc)
  (if (ge b n) acc (qpqb-runm i m (add b 1) n k c md off (str_concat acc (byte_to_str (mod (add (mod (add (mul (add (mul i m) b) k) c) md) off) 256))))))
 ; the exact world: Q4_K at d = dmin = 1 (0x3c00), so every weight sc * nib - mn is an integer in -63..945; Q6_K at d = 1
 ; with its sixteen scales in -29..29 (the byte (v + 227) mod 256 for v in 0..58), so every weight is an integer of
 ; magnitude at most 928
 (defn qpqb-x4 (i) (qpqb-q4x 15360 15360 (qpqb-runm i 13 0 12 89 7 256 0 "") (qpqb-runm i 131 0 128 167 3 256 0 "")))
 (defn qpqb-x6 (i) (qpqb-q6x (qpqb-runm i 131 0 128 89 13 256 0 "") (qpqb-runm i 67 0 64 53 29 256 0 "") (qpqb-runm i 17 0 16 7 3 59 227 "") 15360))
 (defn qpqb-xpool (type i n acc) (if (ge i n) acc (qpqb-xpool type (add i 1) n (append acc (list (if (eq type 12) (qpqb-x4 i) (qpqb-x6 i)))))))
 ; the exactness, read back from the world's bytes through the body's decode (q4m-flat-at / q6m-flat-at): (every weight an
 ; integer, the largest magnitude present) over weights i..255 of the pool's superblocks k..n-1
 (defn qpqb-xread (type pool k n i acc)
  (if (ge k n) acc
   (if (ge i 256) (qpqb-xread type pool (add k 1) n 0 acc)
    (do (let w (if (eq type 12) (q4m-flat-at (nth pool k) 0 i) (q6m-flat-at (nth pool k) 0 i))) (let m (qpqb-abs w))
        (qpqb-xread type pool k n (add i 1) (list (if (and (eq (nth acc 0) 1) (eq w (add (float_to_int w) 0.0))) 1 0) (if (gt m (nth acc 1)) m (nth acc 1))))))))
 ; activations of +-1, 257 of them: -1 where (17 i mod 257) < 128
 (defn qpqb-pm (i acc) (if (ge i 257) acc (qpqb-pm (add i 1) (str_concat acc (md-le32 (md-f32-bits (if (lt (mod (mul i 17) 257) 128) -1.0 1.0)))))))
 ; and read back: every word 0x3f800000 or 0xbf800000
 (defn qpqb-pm? (pm i)
  (if (ge i (div (str_len pm) 4)) 1
   (if (or (eq (ln-u32-le pm (mul 4 i)) 1065353216) (eq (ln-u32-le pm (mul 4 i)) 3212836864)) (qpqb-pm? pm (add i 1)) 0)))
 ; 33 rows of `cols` columns at 33 tokens (two tiles of each), the pool laid end to end: superblock s of row r is
 ; pool[(r * cols / 256 + s) mod n]
 (defn qpqb-wide (ps old type pool n stride cols per sp label)
  (qpqb-pool-tile ps old type pool n stride 33 cols 33 (div cols 256) 1 label per sp))
 ; every run of a list answered ok
 (defn qpqb-oks (rs i) (if (ge i (len rs)) 1 (if (nth (nth rs i) 0) (qpqb-oks rs (add i 1)) 0)))
 ; ---- bit 512: the one-hot world ----
 ; n bytes, every one zero but byte `at`, which is b
 (defn qpqb-one (b at n) (str_concat (qpqb-fill 0 at "") (str_concat (byte_to_str b) (qpqb-fill 0 (sub (sub n at) 1) ""))))
 ; a superblock zero in every byte but its one weight at local index li. Q4_K: d 0x3c01 (1 + 2^-10), dmin +0, sub-block
 ; js = li / 32 at sc 63 and mn 0 (js < 4: scale byte js; from 4 on, the high pair of byte js - 4 and the low nibble of byte
 ; js + 4), its nibble li mod 32 at 15: 63 x 15 x (1 + 2^-10) = 945.9228515625
 (defn qpqb-h4 (li)
  (do (let js (div li 32)) (let q (add (mul (div js 2) 32) (mod li 32)))
      (qpqb-q4x 15361 0
       (if (lt js 4) (qpqb-one 63 js 12) (str_concat (qpqb-one 192 (sub js 4) 8) (qpqb-one 15 (sub js 4) 4)))
       (qpqb-one (if (eq (mod js 2) 0) 15 240) q 128))))
 ; Q6_K: d 0x3c01, every quant at q 0 (nibble 0, high pair 2: the high-bit bytes 0xaa) but weight li (half h, quarter g,
 ; column l) at q 31 (nibble 15, high pair 3), its scale byte h * 8 + 2 g + l / 16 at 127 and every other scale 0:
 ; 127 x 31 x (1 + 2^-10) = 3940.8447265625
 (defn qpqb-h6 (li)
  (do (let h (div li 128)) (let g (div (mod li 128) 32)) (let l (mod li 32)) (let ho (add (mul h 32) l))
      (qpqb-q6x (qpqb-one (if (lt g 2) 15 240) (add (mul h 64) (add l (mul (mod g 2) 32))) 128)
                (str_concat (qpqb-fill 170 ho "") (str_concat (byte_to_str (add 170 (qpqb-p4 g))) (qpqb-fill 170 (sub 63 ho) "")))
                (qpqb-one 127 (add (mul h 8) (add (mul 2 g) (div l 16))) 16) 15361)))
 ; the 257 activations: +-pi (1 + (97 i mod 1021) / 1021) 2^(4 (i mod 9) - 16), the sign alternating
 (defn qpqb-p2 (e) (if (lt e 0) (div 1.0 (qpqb-p2 (sub 0 e))) (if (eq e 0) 1.0 (mul 2.0 (qpqb-p2 (sub e 1))))))
 (defn qpqb-hx (i acc)
  (if (ge i 257) acc
   (qpqb-hx (add i 1) (str_concat acc (md-le32 (md-f32-bits (mul (if (eq (mod i 2) 0) 1.0 -1.0)
    (mul (mul 3.141592653589793 (add 1.0 (div (mul 1.0 (mod (mul i 97) 1021)) 1021.0))) (qpqb-p2 (sub (mul 4 (mod i 9)) 16))))))))))
 ; row r's one weight: local index (37 r + 11) mod 256 of its superblock (7 r + 3) mod nsb
 (defn qpqb-oh-li (r) (mod (add (mul r 37) 11) 256))
 (defn qpqb-oh-put (wh type stride nsb rows r)
  (if (ge r rows) wh
   (do (let w (metal_buf_write wh (mul stride (add (mul r nsb) (mod (add (mul r 7) 3) nsb))) (if (eq type 12) (qpqb-h4 (qpqb-oh-li r)) (qpqb-h6 (qpqb-oh-li r)))))
       (qpqb-oh-put wh type stride nsb rows (add r 1)))))
 ; rows of `cols` columns at 33 tokens: the weights written zero whole, then each row's one superblock; against the attestant
 ; and the scalar reference sp
 (defn qpqb-onehot (ps old type stride rows cols hx sp label)
  (do (let nsb (div cols 256)) (let wh (metal_buf_alloc (mul rows (mul nsb stride))))
      (let z (metal_buf_write wh 0 (qpqb-rep2 (qpqb-fill 0 stride "") (mul rows nsb))))
      (qpqb-tile-run ps old type (qpqb-oh-put wh type stride nsb rows 0) rows cols 33 label hx sp)))
 ; the world read back through the body's decode: superblock sb's (nonzero weights, the last one's index, its value)
 (defn qpqb-oh-read (type sb i acc)
  (if (ge i 256) acc
   (do (let v (if (eq type 12) (q4m-flat-at sb 0 i) (q6m-flat-at sb 0 i)))
       (qpqb-oh-read type sb (add i 1) (if (eq v 0.0) acc (list (add (nth acc 0) 1) i v))))))
 ; how many of the one-weight superblocks li..255 do not hold weight w alone at li
 (defn qpqb-oh-bad (type li w bad)
  (if (ge li 256) bad
   (do (let r (qpqb-oh-read type (if (eq type 12) (qpqb-h4 li) (qpqb-h6 li)) 0 (list 0 -1 0.0)))
       (qpqb-oh-bad type (add li 1) w (if (and (eq (nth r 0) 1) (and (eq (nth r 1) li) (eq (nth r 2) w))) bad (add bad 1))))))
 ; every activation word carries more than a half's eleven significant bits: its f32 significand's low thirteen not all zero
 (defn qpqb-hx-full? (hx i) (if (ge i (div (str_len hx) 4)) 1 (if (eq (mod (ln-u32-le hx (mul 4 i)) 8192) 0) 0 (qpqb-hx-full? hx (add i 1)))))
 ; ---- bit 64: what the pair answers on the non-finite patterns p..hi-1, summed into
 ; (pow2 loop at sign | 0x47800000 | m << 13, as_type +-inf at m 0 and NaN otherwise, NaN payload kept, NaN quieted,
 ; NaN read as the canonical 0x7fc00000); the last three are printed, not claimed
 (defn qpqb-nf (va vb p hi acc)
  (if (ge p hi) acc
   (do (let m (mod p 1024)) (let s (mul (div p 32768) 2147483648))
       (let a (ln-u32-le va (mul 4 p))) (let b (ln-u32-le vb (mul 4 p)))
       (let fa (if (eq a (add s (add 1199570944 (mul m 8192)))) 1 0))
       (let fb (if (eq m 0) (if (eq b (add s 2139095040)) 1 0)
                (if (and (eq (mod (div b 8388608) 256) 255) (gt (mod b 8388608) 0)) 1 0)))
       (let kept (if (and (gt m 0) (eq b (add s (add 2139095040 (mul m 8192))))) 1 0))
       (let quiet (if (and (and (gt m 0) (lt m 512)) (eq b (add s (add 2139095040 (mul (add m 512) 8192))))) 1 0))
       (let canon (if (and (gt m 0) (eq b 2143289344)) 1 0))
       (qpqb-nf va vb (add p 1) hi (list (add (nth acc 0) fa) (add (nth acc 1) fb) (add (nth acc 2) kept) (add (nth acc 3) quiet) (add (nth acc 4) canon))))))
 ; ---- bit 128: the dispatch refuses a K-quant view whose cols is not whole superblocks, before any enqueue ----
 (defn qpqb-refused (ps type cols)
  (do
   (let wh (metal_buf_alloc 8192)) (let x (metal_buf_alloc 8192)) (let y (metal_buf_alloc 64))
   (let sent (qpqb-rep2 (md-le32 (md-f32-bits 42.25)) 16))
   (let w0 (metal_buf_write y 0 sent))
   (let before (nth (metal_live) 7))
   (let r (attempt (q38-mv-batch-y ps (list wh 3 cols type) x y 1 3 0)))
   (let after (nth (metal_live) 7))
   (let synced (metal_sync))
   (let kept (str_eq (metal_buf_read y 0 64) sent))
   (let freed (sum (list (metal_buf_free wh) (metal_buf_free x) (metal_buf_free y))))
   (let why (q38pq-whole-refusal type cols))
   (print (list "k-quant cols refusal: type" type "cols" cols "answered nothing" (if (nothing? r) 1 0) "dispatches before, after" before after "output kept" (if kept 1 0) "freed" freed "named" why))
   (and (nothing? r) (and (eq before after) (and kept (and (eq freed 3) (gt (str_len why) 0)))))))
 ; the unit's references: the per-token lanes, the attestant tiles, and bit 64's probe in the lane's own unit (its
 ; pragma, its compile): code 1 when q4k_f16 and as_type<half> differ in a bit, 2 when q6k_f16 and as_type<half> do,
 ; 4 / 8 / 16 when as_type / q4k_f16 / q6k_f16 read non-finite, 32 when the two software decodes differ; and the bits
 ; of the pow2 loop's reading (va) and as_type's (vb)
 (let refs (str_concat (qml-lane-msl "qpqb_q4" "q4k" "144") (str_concat (qml-lane-msl "qpqb_q6" "q6k" "210")
   (str_concat "kernel void qpqb_f32(device const float* w [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(4)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]], uint lane [[thread_index_in_simdgroup]]) { uint r = gid / 32u; if (r >= rows) return; float a = 0.0f; uint k = (cols > lane) ? ((cols-lane+31u)/32u) : 0u; while(k > 0u) { --k; uint j = lane+k*32u; float p = w[r*cols+j]*x[j]; a = p+a; } float s = metal::simd_sum(a); if (lane == 0u) y[r]=s; }"
    (str_concat (qmb-quant-mma "qpqb_q4k_mma_wi" "q4k" "144" "256") (str_concat (qmb-quant-mma "qpqb_q6k_mma_wi" "q6k" "210" "256")
     "kernel void qpqb_f16 (device uint* code [[buffer(0)]], device uint* va [[buffer(1)]], device uint* vb [[buffer(2)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= 65536u) return; uint ua = as_type<uint>(q4k_f16(int(i))); uint uc = as_type<uint>(q6k_f16(int(i))); uint ub = as_type<uint>(float(as_type<half>(ushort(i)))); va[i] = ua; vb[i] = ub; code[i] = (ua == ub ? 0u : 1u) | (uc == ub ? 0u : 2u) | ((ub & 2139095040u) == 2139095040u ? 4u : 0u) | ((ua & 2139095040u) == 2139095040u ? 8u : 0u) | ((uc & 2139095040u) == 2139095040u ? 16u : 0u) | (ua == uc ? 0u : 32u); }"))))))
 (let msl (str_concat (q38-msl) refs))
 (let ps (q38-pipes msl))
 (let c4 (qpqb-shape ps msl 12 (read_file_slice "form/form-stdlib/tests/fixtures/q4k-two-superblocks.bin" 0 288) 2 256 "qpqb_q4" 1))
 (let c6 (qpqb-shape ps msl 14 (read_file_slice "form/form-stdlib/tests/fixtures/q6k-two-superblocks.bin" 0 420) 2 256 "qpqb_q6" 2))
 (let c8 (qpqb-shape ps msl 8 (read_file_slice "form/form-stdlib/tests/fixtures/q8-0-three-blocks.bin" 0 102) 3 32 "form_q8_0_matvec_lane_f32" 4))
 (let cf (qpqb-shape ps msl 0 (qpqb-input 512 0 "") 2 256 "qpqb_f32" 8))
 (let d4a (qpqb-decode ps 12 "form/form-stdlib/tests/fixtures/q4k-two-superblocks.bin" 144 3 512 1))
 (let d4b (qpqb-decode ps 12 "form/form-stdlib/tests/fixtures/q4k-two-superblocks.bin" 144 257 5120 1))
 (let d6a (qpqb-decode ps 14 "form/form-stdlib/tests/fixtures/q6k-two-superblocks.bin" 210 3 512 3))
 (let d6b (qpqb-decode ps 14 "form/form-stdlib/tests/fixtures/q6k-two-superblocks.bin" 210 257 5120 3))
 (let o4 (metal_pipeline msl "qpqb_q4k_mma_wi"))
 (let o6 (metal_pipeline msl "qpqb_q6k_mma_wi"))
 (let sb4 (read_file_slice "form/form-stdlib/tests/fixtures/q4k-two-superblocks.bin" 0 288))
 (let sb6 (read_file_slice "form/form-stdlib/tests/fixtures/q6k-two-superblocks.bin" 0 420))
 (let per (qpqb-input 257 0 ""))
 (let t4 (list (qpqb-tile ps o4 12 sb4 144 3 9 per) (qpqb-tile ps o4 12 sb4 144 3 33 per) (qpqb-tile ps o4 12 sb4 144 257 9 per) (qpqb-tile ps o4 12 sb4 144 257 33 per)))
 (let t6 (list (qpqb-tile ps o6 14 sb6 210 3 9 per) (qpqb-tile ps o6 14 sb6 210 3 33 per) (qpqb-tile ps o6 14 sb6 210 257 9 per) (qpqb-tile ps o6 14 sb6 210 257 33 per)))
 ; the edge pools: the two committed superblocks first, then the families and the named edges
 (let ff12 (qpqb-fill 255 12 "")) (let ho12 (str_concat (qpqb-fill 192 8 "") (qpqb-fill 0 4 "")))
 (let P4 (append (list (substring sb4 0 144) (substring sb4 144 288))
  (append (qpqb-q4fam 0 0 (list)) (append (qpqb-q4fam 1 0 (list)) (append (qpqb-q4fam 2 0 (list))
   (append (list (qpqb-q4 93 0 0) (qpqb-q4 94 32768 32768) (qpqb-q4 95 1 32769) (qpqb-q4 96 1023 1023)
         (qpqb-q4x 1024 33792 ho12 (qpqb-run 97 0 128 167 3 "")) (qpqb-q4x 31743 64511 ff12 (qpqb-fill 255 128 ""))
         (qpqb-q4x 64511 1 ho12 (qpqb-fill 0 128 "")) (qpqb-q4 100 15360 15360))
    (append (qpqb-q4fam 3 0 (list)) (qpqb-q4fam 4 0 (list)))))))))
 (let P6 (append (list (substring sb6 0 210) (substring sb6 210 420))
  (append (qpqb-q6fam 0 0 (list)) (append (qpqb-q6fam 1 0 (list))
   (list (qpqb-q6x (qpqb-fill 255 128 "") (qpqb-fill 255 64 "") (qpqb-fill 128 16 "") 31743)
         (qpqb-q6x (qpqb-fill 0 128 "") (qpqb-fill 0 64 "") (qpqb-fill 127 16 "") 64511)
         (qpqb-q6x (qpqb-fill 0 128 "") (qpqb-fill 0 64 "") (qpqb-fill 128 16 "") 1)
         (qpqb-q6 65 0) (qpqb-q6 66 32768) (qpqb-q6 67 15360))))))
 (let n4 (len P4)) (let n6 (len P6))
 (let e4 (list (qpqb-pool-tile ps o4 12 P4 n4 144 n4 256 9 1 0 "edge pool" per 0) (qpqb-pool-tile ps o4 12 P4 n4 144 n4 256 33 1 0 "edge pool" per 0) (qpqb-pool-tile ps o4 12 P4 n4 144 n4 512 33 1 1 "edge pool" per 0)))
 (let e6 (list (qpqb-pool-tile ps o6 14 P6 n6 210 n6 256 9 1 0 "edge pool" per 0) (qpqb-pool-tile ps o6 14 P6 n6 210 n6 256 33 1 0 "edge pool" per 0) (qpqb-pool-tile ps o6 14 P6 n6 210 n6 512 33 1 1 "edge pool" per 0)))
 (let z62 (qpqb-fill 48 62 "")) (let z64 (qpqb-fill 48 64 "")) (let z256 (qpqb-fill 48 256 ""))
 (let f62 (qpqb-fill 49 62 "")) (let f64 (qpqb-fill 49 64 "")) (let f256 (qpqb-fill 49 256 ""))
 ; a sign x exponent cell counts in a live row: the attestant's words over the rows of one superblock at 9 tokens
 (let cov4 (qpqb-q4cov P4 0 n4 (list z62 z62 z64 z64 z64 z64) (nth (nth e4 0) 1) (add n4 3) 9))
 (let cov6 (qpqb-q6cov P6 0 n6 (list z62 z256 z64 0 0) (nth (nth e6 0) 1) (add n6 3) 9))
 (let cov4ok (and (and (str_eq (nth cov4 0) f62) (str_eq (nth cov4 1) f62))
                  (and (and (str_eq (nth cov4 2) f64) (str_eq (nth cov4 3) f64)) (and (str_eq (nth cov4 4) f64) (str_eq (nth cov4 5) f64)))))
 (let cov6ok (and (and (str_eq (nth cov6 0) f62) (str_eq (nth cov6 1) f256)) (and (str_eq (nth cov6 2) f64) (and (eq (nth cov6 3) 1) (eq (nth cov6 4) 1)))))
 (print (list "edge pools: Q4_K superblocks" n4 "d alone and live at sign x exponent (+ 0..30, - 0..30)" (nth cov4 0) "dmin alone and live at" (nth cov4 1)
  "sc at sub-blocks 0..3 / 4..7 whole" (str_eq (nth cov4 2) f64) (str_eq (nth cov4 3) f64) "mn whole" (str_eq (nth cov4 4) f64) (str_eq (nth cov4 5) f64)))
 (print (list "edge pools: Q6_K superblocks" n6 "d live at sign x exponent" (nth cov6 0) "scale bytes whole" (str_eq (nth cov6 1) f256)
  "quants -32..31 whole" (str_eq (nth cov6 2) f64) "a superblock of -32, of 31" (nth cov6 3) (nth cov6 4)))
 (let c32 (if (and (and (gt o4 0) (gt o6 0)) (and (and (eq (qpqb-oks t4 0) 1) (eq (qpqb-oks t6 0) 1))
               (and (and cov4ok cov6ok) (and (eq (qpqb-oks e4 0) 1) (eq (qpqb-oks e6 0) 1))))) 32 0))
 ; bit 64: the f16 identity over every pattern
 (let pf (metal_pipeline msl "qpqb_f16"))
 (let fc (metal_buf_alloc (mul 4 65536))) (let fa (metal_buf_alloc (mul 4 65536))) (let fb (metal_buf_alloc (mul 4 65536)))
 ; every slot starts as 0x5a5a5a5a, a finite word none of the checks below accepts: a pattern the probe leaves unwritten
 ; reads short
 (let f5a (qpqb-rep2 (md-le32 1515870810) 65536))
 (let fw (list (metal_buf_write fc 0 f5a) (metal_buf_write fa 0 f5a) (metal_buf_write fb 0 f5a)))
 (let ef (metal_enqueue pf (md-bind (list fc fa fb) (list)) 65536))
 (let sf (metal_sync))
 (let codes (metal_buf_read fc 0 (mul 4 65536))) (let va (metal_buf_read fa 0 (mul 4 65536))) (let vb (metal_buf_read fb 0 (mul 4 65536)))
 (let ffreed (sum (list (metal_buf_free fc) (metal_buf_free fa) (metal_buf_free fb))))
 (let z31744 (qpqb-rep2 (md-le32 0) 31744))
 (let finpos (qpqb-first-diff codes z31744 0 31744))
 (let finneg (qpqb-first-diff (substring codes (mul 4 32768) (mul 4 64512)) z31744 0 31744))
 (let n7 (qpqb-rep2 (md-le32 7) 1024))
 (let nfpos (str_eq (substring codes (mul 4 31744) (mul 4 32768)) n7))
 (let nfneg (str_eq (substring codes (mul 4 64512) (mul 4 65536)) n7))
 (let nf (qpqb-nf va vb 31744 32768 (qpqb-nf va vb 64512 65536 (list 0 0 0 0 0))))
 (let zeros (and (and (eq (ln-u32-le va 0) 0) (eq (ln-u32-le vb 0) 0)) (and (eq (ln-u32-le va (mul 4 32768)) 2147483648) (eq (ln-u32-le vb (mul 4 32768)) 2147483648))))
 (print (list "f16 identity: finite patterns 63488, first mismatch (+, -)" finpos finneg
  "+0 (pow2 loop, as_type)" (ln-u32-le va 0) (ln-u32-le vb 0) "-0" (ln-u32-le va (mul 4 32768)) (ln-u32-le vb (mul 4 32768))))
 (print (list "f16 non-finite 2048: codes as claimed (+, -)" (if nfpos 1 0) (if nfneg 1 0) "pow2 loop finite +-2^16 (1 + m/1024)" (nth nf 0)
  "as_type +-inf at m 0, NaN otherwise" (nth nf 1) "NaN payload kept" (nth nf 2) "quieted" (nth nf 3) "read as the canonical 0x7fc00000" (nth nf 4)))
 (print (list "f16 samples (pow2 loop, as_type): 0x7c00" (ln-u32-le va (mul 4 31744)) (ln-u32-le vb (mul 4 31744))
  "0xfc00" (ln-u32-le va (mul 4 64512)) (ln-u32-le vb (mul 4 64512)) "0x7d00" (ln-u32-le va (mul 4 32000)) (ln-u32-le vb (mul 4 32000))
  "0x7e00" (ln-u32-le va (mul 4 32256)) (ln-u32-le vb (mul 4 32256)) "0xffff" (ln-u32-le va (mul 4 65535)) (ln-u32-le vb (mul 4 65535))))
 (let c64 (if (and (and (gt pf 0) (gt ef 0)) (and (and (lt finpos 0) (lt finneg 0)) (and (and nfpos nfneg)
               (and (and (eq (nth nf 0) 2048) (eq (nth nf 1) 2048)) (and zeros (eq ffreed 3)))))) 64 0))
 ; bit 256: rows of 20, 24 and 68 superblocks; the edge pools against the attestant, the exact world against the attestant
 ; and the scalar reference (pipelines 1 / 3)
 (let pm (qpqb-pm 0 ""))
 (let X4 (qpqb-xpool 12 0 71 (list))) (let X6 (qpqb-xpool 14 0 71 (list)))
 ; the real rows' widths, the widest last
 (let wd (list 5120 6144 17408))
 (let r4 (qpqb-xread 12 X4 0 71 0 (list 1 0.0))) (let r6 (qpqb-xread 14 X6 0 71 0 (list 1 0.0)))
 (let exact (and (and (eq (nth r4 0) 1) (eq (nth r6 0) 1))
                 (and (eq (qpqb-pm? pm 0) 1) (and (lt (mul (nth r4 1) (nth wd 2)) 16777216.0) (lt (mul (nth r6 1) (nth wd 2)) 16777216.0)))))
 (print (list "exact world, read back through the body's decode: every weight an integer (Q4_K, Q6_K)" (nth r4 0) (nth r6 0)
  "the largest magnitude present" (nth r4 1) (nth r6 1) "times the widest row's cols" (nth wd 2) "against 2^24" (mul (nth r4 1) (nth wd 2)) (mul (nth r6 1) (nth wd 2)) 16777216
  "every activation +-1" (qpqb-pm? pm 0) "exact" (if exact 1 0)))
 (let w4 (list (qpqb-wide ps o4 12 P4 n4 144 (nth wd 0) per 0 "pool, 20 superblocks a row") (qpqb-wide ps o4 12 P4 n4 144 (nth wd 1) per 0 "pool, 24 superblocks a row")
               (qpqb-wide ps o4 12 P4 n4 144 (nth wd 2) per 0 "pool, 68 superblocks a row") (qpqb-wide ps o4 12 X4 71 144 (nth wd 0) pm (nth ps 1) "exact, 20 superblocks a row")
               (qpqb-wide ps o4 12 X4 71 144 (nth wd 1) pm (nth ps 1) "exact, 24 superblocks a row") (qpqb-wide ps o4 12 X4 71 144 (nth wd 2) pm (nth ps 1) "exact, 68 superblocks a row")))
 (let w6 (list (qpqb-wide ps o6 14 P6 n6 210 (nth wd 0) per 0 "pool, 20 superblocks a row") (qpqb-wide ps o6 14 P6 n6 210 (nth wd 1) per 0 "pool, 24 superblocks a row")
               (qpqb-wide ps o6 14 P6 n6 210 (nth wd 2) per 0 "pool, 68 superblocks a row") (qpqb-wide ps o6 14 X6 71 210 (nth wd 0) pm (nth ps 3) "exact, 20 superblocks a row")
               (qpqb-wide ps o6 14 X6 71 210 (nth wd 1) pm (nth ps 3) "exact, 24 superblocks a row") (qpqb-wide ps o6 14 X6 71 210 (nth wd 2) pm (nth ps 3) "exact, 68 superblocks a row")))
 (let c256 (if (and exact (and (eq (qpqb-oks w4 0) 1) (eq (qpqb-oks w6 0) 1))) 256 0))
 ; bit 512: the one-hot world at 1, 20, 24 and 68 superblocks a row and the tall shape, 4097 rows of 20, against the attestant
 ; and the scalar reference (pipelines 1 / 3), the world read back first
 (let hx (qpqb-hx 0 ""))
 (let ob4 (qpqb-oh-bad 12 0 945.9228515625 0)) (let ob6 (qpqb-oh-bad 14 0 3940.8447265625 0))
 (let oz4 (nth (qpqb-oh-read 12 (qpqb-fill 0 144 "") 0 (list 0 -1 0.0)) 0)) (let oz6 (nth (qpqb-oh-read 14 (qpqb-fill 0 210 "") 0 (list 0 -1 0.0)) 0))
 (let ohread (and (and (eq ob4 0) (eq ob6 0)) (and (and (eq oz4 0) (eq oz6 0)) (eq (qpqb-hx-full? hx 0) 1))))
 (print (list "one-hot world, read back through the body's decode: superblocks not holding their one weight alone (Q4_K, Q6_K)" ob4 ob6
  "nonzero weights in a zero superblock" oz4 oz6 "every activation past a half's significand" (qpqb-hx-full? hx 0)))
 (let h4 (list (qpqb-onehot ps o4 12 144 33 256 hx (nth ps 1) "one-hot, 1 superblock a row") (qpqb-onehot ps o4 12 144 33 (nth wd 0) hx (nth ps 1) "one-hot, 20 superblocks a row")
               (qpqb-onehot ps o4 12 144 33 (nth wd 1) hx (nth ps 1) "one-hot, 24 superblocks a row") (qpqb-onehot ps o4 12 144 33 (nth wd 2) hx (nth ps 1) "one-hot, 68 superblocks a row")
               (qpqb-onehot ps o4 12 144 4097 (nth wd 0) hx (nth ps 1) "one-hot, tall: 4097 rows of 20 superblocks")))
 (let h6 (list (qpqb-onehot ps o6 14 210 33 256 hx (nth ps 3) "one-hot, 1 superblock a row") (qpqb-onehot ps o6 14 210 33 (nth wd 0) hx (nth ps 3) "one-hot, 20 superblocks a row")
               (qpqb-onehot ps o6 14 210 33 (nth wd 1) hx (nth ps 3) "one-hot, 24 superblocks a row") (qpqb-onehot ps o6 14 210 33 (nth wd 2) hx (nth ps 3) "one-hot, 68 superblocks a row")
               (qpqb-onehot ps o6 14 210 4097 (nth wd 0) hx (nth ps 3) "one-hot, tall: 4097 rows of 20 superblocks")))
 (let c512 (if (and ohread (and (eq (qpqb-oks h4 0) 1) (eq (qpqb-oks h6 0) 1))) 512 0))
 ; bit 128: the refusal, and the widths the lane holds read whole
 (let c128 (if (and (and (qpqb-refused ps 12 384) (qpqb-refused ps 14 640)) (and (qpqb-refused ps 12 255)
                (and (and (eq (str_len (q38pq-whole-refusal 12 5120)) 0) (eq (str_len (q38pq-whole-refusal 14 17408)) 0))
                     (and (and (eq (str_len (q38pq-whole-refusal 12 6144)) 0) (eq (str_len (q38pq-whole-refusal 14 256)) 0)) (eq (str_len (q38pq-whole-refusal 8 48)) 0))))) 128 0))
 (let guard (if (and (and (eq (q38pq-index 99) -1) (eq (q38dq-index 99) -1))
   (and (eq (nth (metal_live) 2) 0) (and (and d4a d4b) (and d6a d6b)))) 16 0))
 (let verdict (sum (list c4 c6 c8 cf guard c32 c64 c128 c256 c512)))
 (if (eq verdict 1023) verdict (form_error (str_concat "qwen prefill quant band failed: " (int_to_str verdict)))))
